    "body": "This PR is a continuation of https://github.com/neovim/neovim/pull/40097\r\nThis PR will not be merged and will be continuously rebased and updated until the migration to `libghostty` is complete.\r\nRef: https://github.com/neovim/neovim/issues/40017\r\n\r\n#### Current status\r\n\r\nThe implementation is _largely complete_. Some testing and documentation still need to finalized.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nfeat(terminal): restore state file with `:edit`\r\n\r\nProblem:\r\nThere is no way to restore a terminal from a saved terminal state file.\r\n\r\nSolution:\r\n- `:edit stdpath('state')/term/*.mpack`: restore a terminal state file in the standard terminal state directory\r\n- `:edit term://{dir}//{cmd}`: restore a live terminal from the matching state file\r\n- `:edit terms://`: browse saved terminal state by opening `stdpath('state')/term/` with the built-in plugin `dir.lua`\r\n- Session and _Shada mark (documented, not built-in)_ integration",
